WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.936
A class diagram summarizes selected structural
facts. Class boxes can show names, attributes

00:00:05.936 --> 00:00:11.485
and operations; visibility symbols communicate
access, while inheritance and interface

00:00:11.485 --> 00:00:16.905
realization express different contracts.
Associations describe relationships between

00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:21.228
instances, with multiplicity constraining how
many may participate.

00:00:21.228 --> 00:00:26.321
The BankAccount and Student–Course examples
connect these symbols to code so that notation

00:00:26.321 --> 00:00:30.226
supports an explanation rather than becoming a
memorization exercise.

00:00:30.228 --> 00:00:35.305
Read multiplicity from the relevant association
end and distinguish capacity from actual

00:00:35.305 --> 00:00:40.381
participation. An array with thirty slots is not
evidence that thirty courses are always

00:00:40.381 --> 00:00:45.112
assigned. Composition expresses strong ownership
in the model, whereas an ordinary

00:00:45.112 --> 00:00:47.708
association need not imply a shared lifetime.

00:00:47.728 --> 00:00:52.649
Nested classes, dependencies and notes add
detail when needed. Correct partial snippets

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:57.683
before treating them as runnable
implementations, and state conventions where the
diagram

00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:02.774
omits information. Does a Student containing a
Course array of length thirty imply exactly

00:01:02.774 --> 00:01:04.132
thirty enrolled courses?

00:01:04.228 --> 00:01:09.976
No. Storage capacity does not establish actual
enrollment; multiplicity should express the

00:01:09.976 --> 00:01:11.701
intended domain constraint.

00:01:11.728 --> 00:01:16.888
UML can be used selectively to resolve a design
question rather than to document every

00:01:16.888 --> 00:01:22.348
implementation detail. The cited industry study
illustrates different usage patterns, not a

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:27.749
universal adoption rate for every team. A
diagram earns its place by helping collaborators

00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:28.169
reason.

00:01:28.228 --> 00:01:33.433
Design patterns likewise provide reusable
language for a problem, a solution structure and

00:01:33.433 --> 00:01:35.457
the consequences that accompany it.

00:01:35.457 --> 00:01:40.717
A pattern is not a mechanical recipe. Its forces
and tradeoffs must fit the system, language

00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:45.691
and expected changes. The architectural-doorway
example makes this concrete: the layout

00:01:45.691 --> 00:01:50.951
responds to patterns of movement rather than to
an abstract preference for doors in corners.

00:01:50.957 --> 00:01:56.221
Composition delegates behavior through
collaborating objects, while inheritance commits
to a

00:01:56.221 --> 00:02:01.485
subtype relationship and its contracts. Prefer
the mechanism that expresses the relationship

00:02:01.485 --> 00:02:06.634
and controls the intended variation. Should
every recurring code fragment be replaced by a

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:07.836
named design pattern?

00:02:07.957 --> 00:02:13.385
No. Use a pattern when its problem and tradeoffs
match; adding structure without a need can

00:02:13.385 --> 00:02:14.280
reduce clarity.

00:02:14.457 --> 00:02:19.749
The single responsibility principle asks whether
a class has one coherent reason to change.

00:02:19.749 --> 00:02:24.925
Responsibilities arise from the concerns and
policies it serves, not simply the number of

00:02:24.925 --> 00:02:29.985
methods. A cohesion graph connecting methods
that share fields can expose clusters, but

00:02:29.985 --> 00:02:31.614
shared state is only a clue.

00:02:31.614 --> 00:02:36.868
Methods can share a field while serving
unrelated purposes, and a coherent
responsibility

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.758
can use several data structures.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:44.083
The split-class exercise asks which changes
should remain independent. Separating storage,

00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:49.527
formatting or domain calculations can reduce the
number of clients affected by a change. The

00:02:49.527 --> 00:02:54.853
historical Date API example illustrates the
long-lived cost of mixing concerns in a public

00:02:54.853 --> 00:02:55.326
library.

00:02:55.326 --> 00:03:00.782
Compatibility limits cleanup after release, so
careful boundaries matter. Avoid splitting

00:03:00.782 --> 00:03:05.809
every method into its own object; the goal is a
coherent model with understandable

00:03:05.809 --> 00:03:11.020
responsibilities and interfaces. If every method
touches the same field, has SRP been

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:11.449
proved?

00:03:11.449 --> 00:03:17.362
No. Shared fields suggest structural cohesion
but do not establish a single policy or reason

00:03:17.362 --> 00:03:18.004
to change.
